    {
      "id": "p0030-b004",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Sometimes a literal translation might sound unintentionally redundant or foolish. This is common in entertainment translation when special terminology is being defined, and said terminology uses words from a foreign language. Redundancy can also occur when a word sounds complicated in the original language but simple in the target language.",
        "raw": "Sometimes a literal translation might sound unintentionally redundant or\nfoolish. This is common in entertainment translation when special terminology\nis being defined, and said terminology uses words from a foreign language.\nRedundancy can also occur when a word sounds complicated in the original\nlanguage but simple in the target language.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29368508,
          0.19853571,
          0.90227437,
          0.28547143
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.29118335,
          0.19782143,
          0.90430007,
          0.28654286
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          7,
          8,
          9,
          10,
          11
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "有时直译会无意间显得重复或可笑。娱乐作品在解释专门术语、而术语又借用了外语词时，这种情况很常见。一个词在原语言里听着复杂，在目标语言里却很简单，也可能造成重复。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
